  str_n7_paper_5_1_title = [[
<size=50><color=#353330>All Hail the Mighty Caelestite
All Hail the Friendships!</color></size>]],
  str_n7_paper_5_2_title = [[
<size=30>Guild Headquarters Steps Up
Underground Auctions Will Return</size>]],
  str_n7_paper_5_3_title = "<size=35><color=#353330>White Flame Mercenaries Recruiting</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_5_4_title = "<size=30><color=#353330>Breaking News! Phantom Wandering Umbraton Streets Identified!</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_5_5_title = [[
<size=30><color=#353330>Blue Lion Guild Faces End
Solus Family Missing</color></size>]],
  str_n7_paper_1_1_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　Thanks to the significant financial contributions of Mr. Rhein from the Blue Lion Guild, a mountain of Nightium now awaits the winner of the upcoming Underground Arena tournament. In response to profuse thanks from the organizers, Rhein claims that this contribution was merely a day's income for the Blue Lions, the legendary commercial giants of Umbraton.\n　　The Underground Arena gets its name not from the fact that it is held below the city's surface but because of its rules, or rather the fact that there are no rules. The victor can sleep on a heap of gold, while the losers... will no longer need to worry about the future. Many of the city's less valiant fighters were once deterred. However, with this year's huge prize pool, every fighter has become a contender overnight. The registration office has been overwhelmed with challengers every day. Some have even started street fights to warm up for the event.\n　　With this grand occasion, the organizer once again thanked Rhein for his help, while the respected Rhein said: \"Don't thank me. I should be thanking you for the passion you've shown for the Underground Arena. I'm pleased to see the excitement the Underground Arena has generated as we endure these dreary days. It doesn't matter whether you take the prize or not, I hope that everyone in Umbraton can forget their troubles and thoroughly enjoy the thrill of the Underground Arena.\"\n　　One cannot help but commend Rhein for his selflessness and love for the Underground Arena. May the Blue Lion Guild prosper and continue to support the event for many years to come!\n </color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_1_2_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　Istvan has been seen wandering in the wilderness outside Umbraton recently, each time in a different location. Fortunately, our reporter honed his tracking skills in the army and was crowned champion of the annual Battlefield Evacuation Marathon. He finally found the Shadowlord in the valley of north Umbraton—it turns out that Istvan is actually a very mysterious and charming man!\n　　Our reporter spared no effort in tracking down Istvan to ask his opinion on the Blue Lion Guild's investment in the Underground Arena. The Shadowlord replied: \"I'll be watching.\"\n　　As we all know, Istvan has always leaned toward banning such competitions. Therefore, many speculators believe that the Blue Lion Guild's significant investment in the Underground Arena is a direct challenge to Istvan's authority. According to the past news, Istvan is bound to compete for control over the Underground Arena. However, after hearing Istvan's reply, traders now believe that the Shadowlord has more important matters in mind, leading them to buy a large number of bonds from the Blue Lion Guild.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_1_3_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　Seventeen years ago, Eraveil was destroyed, and only a few Caelestites, mortal enemies of the Eclipsites, were left alive. The Caelestites possessed powerful psychic abilities and could even affect the hearts of others. Some say that the Caelestites could even turn Aurorians into Eclipsites.\n　　The last Caelestite has now been reported to have arrived in Umbraton with motives yet unknown. All Umbraton residents are recommended to pay special attention to personal safety at all times. If you see the Caelestite, please keep your distance to avoid being psychically possessed or transformed into an Eclipsite.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_1_4_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　The rainy season is coming. Have you found yourself struggling to dry your clothes? In addition to the many other law-abiding services it has to offer you, Odd Jobs, the shop that guarantees your satisfaction every time, has now launched a new Luminatics Drying Service! Whether it's a shirt, coat, furs, knitted scarves, or even a new brand-name leather bag, Taki will use his hot and hearty Luminatics to infuse your possessions with a unique fragrance and have them dry in no time. Smell them and fill your heart with sunshine—breathe in his fragrant aroma and embrace the vitality of eternal summer!\n　　Free Debt Recovery Services for fifty clothes in one receipt. (Gangs of over 100 members as the debtor will be subject to additional fees.)</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_1_5_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　The Miller Guild, with its century-old Umbraton shop, is famous for its professional and high-quality resale service. Due to the increasingly chaotic public security situation in Umbraton recently, most criminals have been using unconventional, unregulated means to sell stolen goods. Some have even been hawking their stolen goods on the street, initiating price wars that have resulted in a significant decrease in the Miller Guild's turnover. In order to save the guild from ruin, Miller III, the guild leader, quickly turned to gamble, and after incurring huge gambling debts, he seems to have absconded and is nowhere to be found.\n　　Now, the Gambling Union has entrusted this newspaper with the right to sell the Miller Guild's illicit goods resale license at a special price. According to reliable sources, the major gangs of Umbraton will hold a joint operation soon to bolster public security in Umbraton and arrest illegal goods merchants. It is hoped that this operation will solve the Miller Guild's core business failure problem.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_2_1_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　The Underground Arena tournament is well underway, and the ferocity of the contenders has begun to spill out of the ring and onto the streets, as several popular challengers have been discovered in the city's alleyways, neutralized by their fellow competitors. The fierce duels of the past few days have brought several fighters with unique skills to the fore, including the most exciting and popular seeded fighter, Becker, successfully promoted to the next round. Few can forget the moment he destroyed the metal handles of the arena gates. Of course, Becker is more than just a charismatic showman—so far, he has also destroyed all of his opponents. That's right, destroyed, not just defeated—all of the challengers unfortunate enough to have faced Becker are now lying in the same room of Umbraton General Hospital and will no longer be able to compete in this tournament.\n　　According to the tournament schedule, concerns now surround Becker's next opponent. The unknown newcomer is rumored to be the sole survivor of the Caelestites. Though we all hope to see a magnificent battle, we also hope that the frail body can stand Becker's solid steel fists!\n　　Of course, this huge difference in strength does not mean the outcome of this battle is already a foregone conclusion! According to research, conventional lifestyle habits can seriously restrict the development of the body, especially in terms of diet. Therefore, we would like to introduce you to Power Punch Protein Powder, developed by the Blue Lion Guild! Chug down your daily dose to reach new heights of physical fitness! Star challenger Becker is the first warrior to try out this product, and its effectiveness is now obvious to anyone who has been following the tournament. Contact us directly to purchase Power Punch Protein Powder today!\n</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_2_2_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　The upper echelons of Umbraton society and celebrities from all circles await an invitation to this rare exclusive salon and banquet in eager anticipation. This high society salon has existed in Umbraton for many years, through the hard times and the good. Since its inception, it has served the pleasures of the elite and celebrities of all kinds, aiming to guide Umbraton to a better and more prosperous future through exchanging ideas between people from various fields.\n　　The organizers will display new works of art at the upcoming salon, including Mountain Roots, The Fish's Breath, Paw Print, and Empty Wisdom. Umbraton celebrities from all fields have been invited to discuss art together, and the organizers are looking forward to their valued evaluations.\n　　We wish the salon organizers and participants a productive night and thank the organizers for their generous sponsorship of this newspaper.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_2_3_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　My cat is missing—words cannot express how important it is to me! Can you please help me? If my cat is returned safely, you will have my thanks, and I'll even give you fifty cups of coffee as a reward!\n　　About My Cat: It is a small black mechanical cat, very lifelike, but with obvious mechanical wiring visible on the damaged section of its front left leg. It has a red ribbon around its neck with a brass name tag attached to it.\n　　Also, its eyes are different colors, and it's gorgeous!\n　　If you have any information, please contact Connolly, owner of the Holiday Café. Thank you very much!</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_2_4_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　The Courier Union, world-renowned professional service provider, believes in providing world-class services to all peace-loving people across Astra. And now, after several months of preparation, the Courier Union is ready to launch a new decoration service! Whether you live in a single room or a mansion, the Courier Union's decoration team can provide you a full range of services from design and procurement, to construction and evaluation. We promise, if the service fails to achieve the desired effect, redecoration is free of charge!\n　　If you order decoration services via our newspaper, you can save an extra 50 Nightium on top of your 20% discount! This event is limited to this month only, so make sure you place your order as soon as possible! Please contact the Umbraton representative, Eho, for more details!</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_2_5_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>Multiple outlets belonging to The Lin Guild have been closed, with their reopening time yet determined.\n　　Recently, we conducted an on-the-spot investigation into rumors surrounding the closure of multiple shops belonging to The Lin Guild. We can now report that these shops have indeed been closed. These closures were not announced in advance, resulting in significant losses for many of their customers. Those familiar with this matter suspect that the Lin family is planning a conspiracy, but exactly when these shops will resume operation is completely unknown.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_3_1_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　\"The Caelestite is more like a chicken than a teammate,\" Becker shouted before the match.\n　　However, one can never be too sure in the heat of competition. Under the Caelestite's command, the whole team moved like the wind, coordinated perfectly, and attacked ferociously. If Becker hadn't stopped the game by accidentally knocking the judge out mid-fight, he would have fallen in the first round of attacks.\n　　After the match was resumed, Becker dodged before the Caelestite's turn to attack, but he suddenly screamed in pain and fell to the ground, foaming at the mouth. He then began trembling all over and was soon carried off the battlefield. According to the doctor on-site, Becker seemed to have been asked by the sponsor to take Power Punch Protein Powder in the middle of the competition. It led to abdominal cramps and triggered a stress-induced abdominal muscle spasm, forcing him to swallow the bitterness of defeat. Some also say that the Caelestite saw that Becker was having trouble fighting and used some underhanded trickery to cause Becker to cramp up. Whatever the truth of the matter, this emergency caused panic among many contestants who use the same product.\n　　Our reporter stated that silence gripped the arena after the Caelestite's unexpected victory. The only person who began laughing as wildly as Becker had done before the fight was Miller III. It turns out that, in his desperation, he gambled all he had on the Caelestite. The outrageous odds before the match earned him a vast fortune, and he then exclaimed, \"The Miller Guild is ready to sell back all outstanding stolen goods!\"\n </color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_3_2_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　Reporter: Hello, Lady Sheol. The Cloudrover Guild recently started propaganda that says \"free gift-pack.\" The whole Umbraton is raving about it, as money grows on trees. Can you tell us about the logic behind this business move?\n　　Sheol: Of course. First of all, thank you for supporting the Cloudrover Guild. The idea behind this was to show our gratitude. This is why the guild decided to provide everyone with these gift packs.\n　　Reporter: Many investors believe that this move by the Cloudrover Guild will lead to losses. However, the results have left them speechless—the Cloudrover Guild's income has increased! Can you tell us why?\n　　Sheol: We have strengthened the public image of the Cloudrover Guild. As a result, we will further upgrade the gift packs to \"Gift Packs—Plus\"! Every Umbraton resident will get one for free, with no additional condition attached!\n　　Conclusion: Glory to the Cloudrover Guild! Although they're giving out gift packs, many people have been inspired to spend even more after opening theirs. An endless stream of people has been flooding the Cloudrover Guild to buy more of their products. Now, it's time for the reporters to go pick up his gift pack!</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_3_3_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　Yesterday, a group of mutated Eclipsites suddenly attacked several trucks. These Eclipsites hiding in the shadows exhibited strange forms and infinite power. They may have been experimental results of some unknown mad scientist from Lumopolis. Our Umbraton is now under dual threats of Lumopolis and enhanced Eclipsites!\n　　During the attack, someone wisely sprinkled St. John's Eclipsite-eradicating powder on the Eclipsites. The Eclipsites immediately covered their faces and screamed as they ran away. All those present survived.\n　　St. John's Eclipsite Eradicating powder is made through 88 elaborate processes, and is an essential medicine for anyone, both at home and away, to fight off the evils.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_3_4_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　According to the latest internal reports, Rhein, the leader of the Blue Lion Guild, one of the town's most prosperous in recent years, seems to be actively contacting Istvan in private, hoping for the peaceful coexistence of the two parties in the future. Istvan also seems to have replied in goodwill.\n　　Although the power struggle between the Blue Lion Guild and the Guild Headquarters led by Istvan has promoted prosperity and development in Umbraton, it has also objectively caused many social problems. Some critics believe that this is an important step in establishing true peace in Umbraton, symbolizing reconciliation between the new and old forces of the town.\n　　Some also believe that this is just a smokescreen for both sides. We are now witnessing the calm before the storm as a bigger conspiracy brew.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_3_5_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　According to reliable sources, the Solus family has recently recruited troops in secret to form a professional team skilled in covert operations and has even recruited Mund, the Stealth King. Rumors abound that the mysterious disappearance of many dignitaries from Umbraton and Lumopolis is inextricably linked to Mund. At present, several members suspected of having a conflict of interest with community organizations have vanished.\n　　The professional team assembled by the Solus family may soon shake up Umbraton's current order.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_4_1_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　The Dam of Scars has been sabotaged. This shocking news has spread throughout Umbraton and caused great commotion in the city. However, we can confidently report that the culprit behind the dam's destruction was none other than the leader of the Blue Lion Guild, Rhein, who has already been brought to justice by Umbraton's faithful protector, Istvan.\n　　When the ensuing flood rushed toward Umbraton, Istvan once again stood firmly against the tide. He commanded his mercenaries to drain and redirect water from the region and help residents escape from the danger zone. Also, Istvan coordinated his forces with the Cloudrover Guild to rescue the wounded. He then sent his gang to end Solus and his followers, who planned to use this opportunity to destroy Umbraton. Thanks to Istvan's wise leadership, Umbraton survived this crisis with minimal losses. Let us once again thank Istvan for his selfless dedication to Umbraton.\n　　May Istvan continue to safeguard Umbraton, now and forevermore faithfully.\n</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_4_2_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　It is only natural to root for the dark horse. The Caelestite has won all of the battles for several consecutive days. Now, all eyes are on the last Caelestite proceeding through the tournament, becoming one of the most popular players on the battlefield. The supporters, who collectively call themselves \"Lovegators,\" have now grown considerably.\n　　But let us focus now on events occurring outside the arena. The Caelestite's supporters have unfortunately been causing disturbances on the streets, engaging in frequent clashes with the supporters of other players over the past two days. Last night, they even initiated violence among the crowd spectating the event, causing widespread chaos. According to reports, the Caelestite was personally unaware of these events. However, it is still not difficult to see that the emergence of the Caelestite dark horse has intensified the inherent differences existing among supporters. Most of the Caelestite's supporters are young people eager for change, while the supporters clashing with them belong to the old school, looking forward to returning the arena's reigning champion.\n　　With friction between the two sides existing for some time now, the emergence of the Caelestite has only added fuel to the fire, resulting in an inferno readying to reach fever pitch. How far can this dark horse go? Let's wait and see.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_4_3_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　The territory controlled by the fierce Spearows has been awarded Umbraton's Public Security Award once more. When our reporter interviewed Dayna and Robyn to ask them how the Spearows has managed to apprehend dozens of street-level gangsters each week consistently, the modest young leaders had this to say: \"These fools out on the street are always trying to hurt Robyn... Hey! You over there! What are you looking at?!\"\n　　Let us thank Dayna and Robyn for their outstanding contribution to community safety.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_4_4_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　It is reported that Rhein had been secretly conducting illegal auctions under the guise of holding frequent salons. Our reporters have confirmed that all related persons of interest have been arrested.\n　　This newspaper hereby declares that we had no acknowledgment of the illegal acts perpetrated by the Blue Lion Guild. All related reports published for the salon in the past were above-board and for commercial purposes only. In the future, all content will be monitored and verified more strictly to avoid disseminating information that may have an adverse effect on Umbraton society.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_4_5_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　A large number of enhanced Eclipsite bodies have been found in the alley next to the Cornwall Cafe on Cross Street. A waiter at the cafe told us that she heard a strange noise when closing up last night. From the shop window, she witnessed a muscular man in a Lumo Hall of Justice uniform throwing dying Eclipsites into the alley one at a time.\n　　These bodies have now begun to decay, creating a pungent smell in the surrounding area. The man responsible is urged to contact the Umbraton Street Sanitation Office as soon as possible to pay the corresponding disposal fees and related fines. Otherwise, Umbraton will have no choice but to file charges against the Lumo Hall of Justice for polluting the environment.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_5_1_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　We have just witnessed a fiercely thrilling tournament, thanks to the dark horse, or should we say, thanks to the almighty Caelestite! Thank you for providing us with such an incredible spectacle!\n　　By observing the previous games, purchasing information on the black market, and eavesdropping, many strong contenders for the championship learned about the Caelestite's tactics. Therefore, when faced with the trenchant attacks of the Caelestite's team, these contenders failed to adopt a conservative and clear strategy, instead choosing to attack head-on! After these wild, desperate attacks, they paid the ultimate price for their rashness and will be contemplating their decision in the local hospital!\n　　Without failing the hopes of the Lovegators! Without letting any chance to the opponents! Long live the Caelestite! Facing opponents' targeted strategies and insidious schemes, there was no complaint about their shenanigans to the referee. And our Caelestite demonstrated a majestic flair for tactics and leadership inherited from the great Caelestite commanders once present in Lumopolis, Illumina, Eraveil, Umbraton, and Northland. Seizing the moment to claim victory! The glorious tradition of the Caelestites!\n　　Truly one in a million, our Caelestite possesses the power to perceive opportunities to strike that most ordinary people could never seize in a lifetime of battles—opportunities that come along once in a thousand years! Now, the Caelestite is not fighting alone—glorious Navigator, the victory is yours!\n　　With the power to take enemies down in one decisive strike, all it takes is one command! One devastating attack! Leaving the foes without even the slightest chance to react! With everyone in the crowd bearing witness! The Caelestite claimed victory—not just personal, but for the fellow Caelestites, the team, the Underground Arena, Istvan, Umbraton, and everyone around the world who loves the thrill of combat! Long live the Caelestite!\n　　*We would like to take this opportunity to apologize to all readers. We have not seen such an exciting tournament in a long time. As the reporter who witnessed the final battle fainted with excitement after writing the above live report, the editor-in-chief has taken it upon himself to continue writing this article.\n　　Following the Caelestite's victory, Istvan presented our winner with a belt, representing ultimate supremacy in the Underground Arena, thus securing a place in the hall of fame for the Caelestite! When the belt raised high, the audience exploded in a raucous round of applause. Moreover, the cheers resonated throughout the arena for what seemed like an eternity.\n　　Almighty Caelestite champion, you will forever have a place in the heart of each and every Umbraton people!\n</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_5_2_content = "<size=35><color=#353330>　　The underground auctions were suspended due to the recent rebellion. Now it has been outlawed due to their inextricable relationship with Rhein. After learning this unfortunate news, both buyers and sellers clamored in outrage that they would no longer have the opportunity to procure the rare auction items on offer nor reap financial benefits from these auctions—a double blow dealt with all concerned.\n　　Amid the doom and gloom surrounding the situation, Bethel proposed that the Umbraton Guild Headquarters faithfully revive these underground auctions. Yes, that is right—a faithful revival! She promised to continue hosting the auctions, providing a new venue, publicity, and security, leading Umbraton's despondent buyers and sellers to see the light of hope finally.\n　　After this, under the supervision of the Guild Headquarters, the first auction was held in Umbraton Square. As everyone heard the echoing sound of the falling hammer, the event was officially recognized as an aboveground auction. Bethel also announced that, from that day on, the aboveground auction would be open to everyone. Everyone can join in, as long as you submit an application to the Guild Headquarters and receive authorization, without any additional conditions! Those involved with the original auctions were left weeping tears of joy upon hearing the news. They applauded Bethel's decision and announced that they would be proud to participate in the new aboveground auctions.\n　　Long live the aboveground auction! Long live free trade! Long live Bethel!</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_5_3_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　Boundless credibility! Battle powers, skill, and experience are all virtues that can be cultivated, but no virtue is more difficult to refine than credibility. In this mercenary squad, you can safely rely on your allies and have them treat you in kind.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_5_4_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　Residents of Cross Street, have you heard strange laughter echoing through the streets late at night? The source of this laughter was a dark shadow recently spotted lurking at the end of the street. Was this shadow an aberration of Aurorian nature? Or the embodiment of our collectively declining morality? We will now solve this riddle, exclusively for you—this shadow haunting Umbraton in the dead of night was, in fact, none other than Miller III.\n　　Miller III, who placed an extremely large bet on the Caelestite's victory, recently lost his investment due to the collapse of the Blue Lion Guild. He was also apparently dealt a severe blow to his ego and resorted to wandering Umbraton at night like a restless wraith.\n　　When our reporter finally cornered him and asked him how he felt about the Caelestite's victory, he suddenly screamed and ran away. All our reporter managed to find of him was a shoe missing its laces by the riverside. Miller III, the inheritor of the century-old guild, is now missing, presumed dead.\n　　Dream chasers like him appear in Umbraton every day. As long as you can adapt to the unwritten rules of Umbraton, this can be a blissful place. Fail to do so, and an unfortunate fate awaits you. Ah, the beautiful and mysterious Umbraton—a place of hopes, desires, and endless dreams.</color></size>",
  str_n7_paper_5_5_content = "<size=28><color=#353330>　　It was once deemed respectable for residents of Umbraton to obtain a position within the Blue Lion Guild. Now the Blue Lion Guild has become the object of the city's scorn. Its members have abandoned their once-proud brooches and defected to join other guilds in the hopes of surviving in Umbraton.\n　　The Solus family, instigators of the recent tumult, have disappeared and most likely fled Umbraton. Anonymous sources are now offering a high price for information on the Solus family. If you know their current whereabouts or status, dead or alive, please inform this newspaper immediately.</color></size>",
